import ../../../testing/driver.dl
import ../../../ui/services.dl

class:
    patterns:
        test capabilities
    members:
        calls as an integer
        requests as an integer
        cancellations as an integer

to get [call test capability] {a pointer:context} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [named] {C string:name} [containing] {string:payload}:
    set state to context as a pointer to test capabilities
    increment state's calls
    require condition (name = "storage") reporting "A service call changed its name."
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI call result, true, (payload + "-stored"))

to get [request test capability] {a pointer:context} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [named] {C string:name} [containing] {string:payload}:
    set state to context as a pointer to test capabilities
    increment state's requests
    require condition (name = "language") reporting "A service request changed its name."
    queue UI input of kind 11 key (state's requests) at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing payload in view
    return state's requests

to get [cancel test capability] {a pointer:context} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [numbered] {integer:request}:
    set state to context as a pointer to test capabilities
    increment state's cancellations
    return request = state's requests

document example:
    paragraph "Status" containing "Host capabilities" using no UI appearance

set instance to an instance of example
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 900 by 600 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
set state to a new test capabilities
set provider to @intrinsic("construct", UI service provider, (the address of state) as a pointer,
    the function named "call test capability $ in $ named $ containing $",
    the function named "request test capability $ in $ named $ containing $",
    the function named "cancel test capability $ in $ numbered $")
set services to the address of provider
set result to a UI call named "storage" containing "data" through services in (the address of view)
set following to a UI call named "storage" containing "next" through services in (the address of view)
require condition (result's success and (result's contents = "data-stored")) reporting "A subsequent call invalidated an owned result."
require condition (following's success and (following's contents = "next-stored")) reporting "A synchronous service lost its payload or owned result."
set request to a UI request named "language" containing "reply" through services in (the address of view)
require condition (request = 1) reporting "An asynchronous service lost its request identity."
require condition ((view's input first's key = request) and (view's input first's text = "reply")) reporting "A service reply did not enter the shared event stream."
require condition (cancel UI request request through services in (the address of view)) reporting "A service could not cancel its own request."
require condition ((state's calls = 2) and ((state's requests = 1) and (state's cancellations = 1))) reporting "Service contexts were not retained."
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Host capabilities use one transport contract independently of the renderer."
